A practical low-level timer primitive balances simplicity and concurrency correctness without advanced lock-free tricks. It exercises circular data structures, wrap-around logic, and safe locking choices.

## Key Concepts
- Circular buffers and wrap-around
- Basic thread-safety with mutexes
- Timer expiry semantics and id-based cancellation
- Correct test coverage for races and timing drift

