## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of atomic operations, memory ordering, and cache behavior. A ticket lock is simple yet reveals reasoning about spin-waiting and fairness.

## Key Concepts

- Atomic operations and memory_order semantics
- FIFO fairness and starvation risk
- Cache-line padding to avoid false sharing
- Busy-wait vs back-off strategies

## Code Example

```c
#include <stdatomic.h>
typedef struct {
  _Atomic_uint next;
  _Atomic_uint serve;
} ticket_lock_t;

void lock(ticket_lock_t *t){
  unsigned my = atomic_fetch_add(&t->next, 1);
  while(atomic_load_explicit(&t->serve, memory_order_acquire) != my) {
    // optional pause
  }
}

void unlock(ticket_lock_t *t){
  atomic_fetch_add(&t->serve, 1);
}
```

